    "answerText": "The answer below lists only claims checked against ScholarChain graph evidence.\n\nClaims:\n- [claim-1] Kele Xu's community in the 2021-2023 window has 116 members. (Uncertainty: Community membership is approximate because label propagation did not fully settle.)\n- [claim-2] Kele Xu has 82 distinct coauthors in 2021-2023, a measure of collaboration breadth.\n- [claim-3] Kele Xu's cross-community degree is 45 and the number of communities connected is 10 in 2021-2023. (Uncertainty: Bridge position uses approximate communities; no betweenness centrality is computed.)\n- [claim-4] Kele Xu's participation coefficient in 2021-2023 is 0.7071, indicating ties spread across several communities. (Uncertainty: Communities are approximate because label propagation did not fully settle.)\n- [claim-5] Kele Xu's connected component in 2021-2023 has a size of 83688.\n- [claim-6] Ming Feng is Kele Xu's strongest 2021-2023 tie, with 4 joint publications from 2022 to 2023.\n- [claim-7] Boqing Zhu shares 3 joint publications with Kele Xu, all in 2022.\n- [claim-8] Hengxing Cai shares 3 joint publications with Kele Xu, from 2022 to 2023.\n- [claim-9] Dawei Feng shares 2 joint publications with Kele Xu, all in 2022.\n- [claim-10] Huaimin Wang 0001 shares 2 joint publications with Kele Xu, from 2022 to 2023.\n- [claim-11] The identity match for Kele Xu is accepted with confidence 0.9500 and 51 publications in the full 2015-2025 window.\n\nMissing evidence (model-written, not verified):\n- Betweenness centrality, which is not computed\n- Settled community assignments, since label propagation did not fully converge\n\nNotes:\n- 'Kele Xu' was resolved to Kele Xu (researcher:v1:0b483e06c74206594317cf2cd77e891f).\n- Bridge position is measured by the number of other communities a researcher's coauthors belong to (communities connected) and the cross-community degree; no betweenness centrality is computed, and communities come from label propagation that did not fully settle, so they are approximate.\n- The model summary contained numbers, identifiers or names not in the graph evidence and was replaced; facts appear only in verified claims.\n- 2 missing-evidence note(s) contained numbers, identifiers or names not in the graph evidence and were left out.",
